==Solution 14 (Menelaus)== 
Let <imath>AC=2</imath>, <imath>AB=1</imath>, hence <imath>BC=\sqrt{3}</imath>. If we use the diagram in Solution 1, first note that <imath>\triangle ACB \sim \triangle ABD</imath> by AA with similar ratio 2, hence <imath>AD=\frac{1}{2}</imath>. Now, we use Menelaus' Theorem in <imath>\triangle BAD</imath> with transversal line <imath>EFC</imath>:
<cmath>\frac{BE}{EA}\cdot \frac{AC}{CD} \cdot \frac{DF}{FB}=1</cmath>
<cmath>\implies \frac{1}{1} \cdot \frac{2}{\frac{3}{2}} \cdot \frac{x}{y}=1</cmath>
<cmath>\implies \frac{x}{y}=\frac{3}{4}</cmath>
So <imath>\frac{x}{x+y}=\boxed{\frac{3}{7} (A)}</imath>.

